 "note": "Busselton Court House and Police Complex, 4 Queen Street (State Register), from the Landgate aerial (Oct 2026), street photos and the inHerit record. The 1897 red-brick court house (hip roof with a ventilator lantern, a half-timbered gable bay, the maroon-and-cream verandah the cafe uses), the 1873 limestone post office beside it, the police office behind, the long limestone cells and stables range running back with its dark lean-to, and the 1906 brick police cottages to the south (marked outbuilding so they don't move the centre). Signs are plain lettering only. Metres: x left to right as seen from Queen Street (south to north), y back from the front of the court house gable bay.",
